  8. Whenever an order has already been refunded, refuse the refund request. For an order that has not yet been delivered, the owner has set no rule, so the refund outcome is undecided.
  9. Whenever an order is placed, it earns one point for every full ₹100 paid for the items after the discount code is applied (for example, ₹1,000 earns 10 points). Exceptions: an order under ₹500 earns 0 points (for example, ₹250 earns 0 points), an order paid with store credit earns 0 points, and a final-sale order earns double the points. No rule has been set for what happens to earned points when a refund occurs.
  10. Whenever the daily sales report is produced, "Orders" is the number of every order in the list, whatever its status (cancelled, unpaid, waiting for payment or paid). "Revenue" is the sum, over card orders only, of the items total after discount plus shipping. "Average" is revenue divided by the number of card orders, rounded down to whole rupees, or 0 if there are no card orders. Cancelled, unpaid and waiting orders are not treated differently beyond these definitions. Refunds are left out of the report and are not deducted from any figure (for example, a fully refunded ₹1,000 order still counts as an order, and a ₹2,000 card order with ₹500 refunded still counts at its full total).
